# The application's environment for deploy/compose.yaml. A TEMPLATE: it holds no real value.
#
#   1. Copy it to a file OUTSIDE the repository checkout and the Docker build context, readable
#      by the operator only:
#          install -m 600 deploy/house-helper.env.example ~/deploy-overlays/secrets/house-helper.env
#      and point Compose at it:  export HOUSE_HELPER_ENV_FILE=~/deploy-overlays/secrets/house-helper.env
#      (the default, deploy/house-helper.env, is git-ignored, but outside the checkout is better).
#   2. Fill in the values. No quotes, no spaces, no trailing spaces; a value that contains a
#      dollar sign must have it doubled ($$), because Compose interpolates this file.
#   3. Never paste a value into a chat, a ticket or a log, and never commit this file filled in.
#
# An empty value counts as not set. As it stands this file starts the application with Telegram
# login off and the assistant unavailable: the page loads, nobody can sign in.
#
# Set by deploy/compose.yaml, and NOT to be set here (compose.yaml wins over this file):
#   HOUSE_HELPER_DATABASE_URL   sqlite:////data/house_helper.db   (the volume; absolute)
#   HOUSE_HELPER_PUBLIC_URL     https://<HOUSE_HELPER_HOST>        (house.elivcloud.org; no path)
#
# Deliberately absent: BOT_TOKEN (the web application has none and asks for none) and every
# HOUSE_HELPER_SMTP_* / HOUSE_HELPER_EMAIL_FROM variable (email login stays off: with none of
# them set the email routes answer 503 and the page draws no email form).

# --- Telegram sign-in (OpenID Connect), from @BotFather -> the bot -> Login Widget -------------
# All of CLIENT_ID and CLIENT_SECRET, or none; a half-set pair stops the application at start.
# The redirect URI to register is  https://house.elivcloud.org/auth/telegram/callback
HOUSE_HELPER_TELEGRAM_CLIENT_ID=
HOUSE_HELPER_TELEGRAM_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Only if @BotFather is set to something other than RS256: ES256 or EdDSA.
# HOUSE_HELPER_TELEGRAM_ID_TOKEN_ALG=RS256

# --- The assistant (OpenAI) ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPENAI_API_KEY is the only required one; without it a chat message is answered 503.
# The rest are optional; the values below are the application's own defaults.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4.1-mini
TEMPERATURE=0.7
MAX_TOKENS=1000
OPENAI_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=15
OPENAI_MAX_RETRIES=1

# GPT-6 Luna (a reasoning model): delete the OPENAI_MODEL, MAX_TOKENS, OPENAI_TIMEOUT_SECONDS lines above and
# set these instead. Needs an image built from the commit that added OPENAI_REASONING_EFFORT: an older image
# ignores the variable and sends `temperature` to a model that does not take it.
#   OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-6-luna
#   OPENAI_REASONING_EFFORT=low     (none, low, medium, high, xhigh; REQUIRED for a gpt-6* model, else no start)
#   MAX_TOKENS=6000                 (reasoning + answer together, sent as max_completion_tokens)
#   OPENAI_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=50       (the chat gives up on the provider after 60 s whatever this says)
#   OPENAI_MAX_RETRIES=1
# TEMPERATURE is not sent while OPENAI_REASONING_EFFORT is set (low, medium, high, xhigh).
